                <title><![CDATA[【Albums (lossless)】PACK - Jethro Tull - 20 Years Of Jethro Tull: The Definitive Collection [Vinyl,5xLP BoxSet] (1988) Hi-Res]]></title>
                <link><![CDATA[https://sharemania.us/threads/jethro-tull-20-years-of-jethro-tull-the-definitive-collection-vinyl-5xlp-boxset-1988-hi-res.290901/]]></link>
                <description><![CDATA[<article>
				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<div style="text-align: center"><b>Jethro Tull - 20 Years Of Jethro Tull: The Definitive Collection [Vinyl,5xLP BoxSet] (1988) Hi-Res</b><br>
<br>
<a href="https://pixhost.to/show/11026/672574022_9efa4850d58ab89e18eed38a0782dbb3.jpg" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://t1.pixhost.to/thumbs/11026/672574022_9efa4850d58ab89e18eed38a0782dbb3.jpg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://t1.pixhost.to/thumbs/11026/672574022_9efa4850d58ab89e18eed38a0782dbb3.jpg"></a><br>
<br>
This really is a fantastic set. I'm new to Tull and have only enjoyed the the pure 70's albums so far and this seems to fill all the gaps between albums. The few later albums and live concerts I have heard have been a bit lacking. It seems to me that the 70's were golden but everything else is for fanatics not purists. That said the Ian Anderson Solo electropop album wasn't half bad and I will be playing it again.<br>
<br>
<b>FLAC (tracks) | Bitrate: Lossless 24bit/96kHz<br>
Genre: Prog Rock | Duration: 03:51:49 | Size: 4.57 GB <br>
<br>
Tracklist:</b><br>
